invariant: INV-14
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: ch_srv_check signs with the private key and then ignores the
  verifier's verdict, so a slot whose public key belongs to another key
  pair boots. The check exists to catch exactly that pairing, which no
  later call can: a server reads no byte of its own chain, so the first
  report of a mismatched identity would otherwise be a client rejecting
  every CertificateVerify. test/srv_auth_test.c gives the ECDSA slot the
  point of a different key pair and requires CH_EINVAL.

--- old
    if (!verify_digest(id, sigalg, digest, sig, sig_len)) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
--- new
    (void)verify_digest(id, sigalg, digest, sig, sig_len);
